From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:16:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] event: keep Xlib's screen size in step with the root window's

JWM restarts in place on the same connection when the root window changes
size, and the restart takes the size from DisplayWidth/DisplayHeight,
which Xlib keeps from the time the connection was opened.  So after a
resize and back to the size of that time JWM saw no change: no restart, the
tray and the background command left as they were.  The Screen structure
gets the new size from the ConfigureNotify, as XRRUpdateConfiguration does; the size in millimetres in
proportion, from the values at start, since Xft takes its DPI from it.
---
 src/event.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/event.c b/src/event.c
index 04335a5..d4530dc 100644
--- a/src/event.c
+++ b/src/event.c
@@ -903,6 +903,28 @@ char HandleConfigureNotify(const XConfigureEvent *event)
       return 0;
    }
    if(rootWidth != event->width || rootHeight != event->height) {
+      /* Xlib's screen size too (as XRRUpdateConfiguration does): the restart
+       * below reads it with DisplayWidth/DisplayHeight on this connection,
+       * which otherwise keeps the size of the time it was opened, and the next
+       * change back to that size would go unnoticed (no restart, no new
+       * background from the background command). */
+      Screen *sp = ScreenOfDisplay(display, rootScreen);
+      static int w0, h0, mw0, mh0;
+      if(!w0) {
+         w0 = sp->width;
+         h0 = sp->height;
+         mw0 = sp->mwidth;
+         mh0 = sp->mheight;
+      }
+      if(w0 > 0 && h0 > 0) {
+         /* the millimetres in proportion, from the size at start (no rounding
+          * adds up): the server keeps the resolution, and Xft takes its DPI
+          * from them */
+         sp->mwidth = (int)((long)mw0 * event->width / w0);
+         sp->mheight = (int)((long)mh0 * event->height / h0);
+      }
+      sp->width = event->width;
+      sp->height = event->height;
       rootWidth = event->width;
       rootHeight = event->height;
       shouldRestart = 1;
